        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "Loose Commentary",
            "block_bbox": [
                92,
                995,
                308,
                1022
            ],
            "block_id": 17,
            "block_order": 16,
            "group_id": 17,
            "global_block_id": 17,
            "global_group_id": 17,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    92.0,
                    995.0
                ],
                [
                    308.0,
                    995.0
                ],
                [
                    308.0,
                    1022.0
                ],
                [
                    92.0,
                    1022.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Loose commentary, which you can think of as an aside or elaboration, differs from an interruption because you can usually move an interruption elsewhere in a sentence. But loose commentary modifies what it stands next to, so it usually cannot be moved. It still needs to be set off with paired commas, parentheses, or dashes, unless it comes at the end of a sentence. In that case, replace the second comma or dash with a period.",
            "block_bbox": [
                91,
                1030,
                784,
                1158
            ],
            "block_id": 18,
            "block_order": 17,
            "group_id": 18,
            "global_block_id": 18,
            "global_group_id": 18,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    91.0,
                    1030.0
                ],
                [
                    784.0,
                    1030.0
                ],
                [
                    784.0,
                    1158.0
                ],
                [
                    91.0,
                    1158.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "It is difficult to explain exactly what counts as loose commentary because it depends on both grammar and meaning. One familiar distinction is between restrictive clauses and nonrestrictive clauses (see pp. 10–11), including appositives.",
            "block_bbox": [
                90,
                1161,
                784,
                1236
            ],
            "block_id": 19,
            "block_order": 18,
            "group_id": 19,
